{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat /work/board.md; printf '\\\\n[sol] 2026-10-22: Key proof: shift q=p-l, l_i=VCG_i, caps h_i=v_i-l_i=min(v_i,D), total t=sum h-D. Vickrey nearest minimizes ||q|| and equals capped waterfill min(lambda,h_i). Full-dimensional centroid strictly below every cap, so equality implies uniform q=t/3. Centroid of capped simplex has E[q_i]<E[q_j] whenever h_i<h_j and h_i<t (pairwise swap/conditional interval proof). Therefore equality iff all h_i equal OR min h_i>=t. This simplifies (positive vi) to all vi equal OR P<=min vi OR P>=sum vi-min vi.\\\\n' >> /work/board.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
